+## Notes, second agent
+
+Picked up after the first agent was stopped. Its partial work was already
+committed (3bc6a43); the working tree was clean apart from this Issue file.
+Two defects fixed on top, both proven by the test suite:
+
+- The deadlock the first agent found was real: `acceptAnswer` drained
+  synchronously on the idle path before `answer()` had registered its
+  waiter, so `resume()` never settled. Fix: acceptance and the processing
+  kick are now separate steps (`kickProcessing`), and `answer()` registers
+  the waiter between them.
+- The server's 202 carried `latest` read after the accept, but an idle
+  accept processes synchronously and the fresh drive's first emit had
+  already broadcast the post-processing state. The server now captures the
+  snapshot before the accept: acceptance never mutates PoolState, so that
+  snapshot still shows the interrupt pending, which is the truthful
+  acceptance-time view.
+
+`bun test` (276 pass) and `bun run typecheck` both green. UI untouched.
+
+---
+
